  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) During early Drosophila gastrulation, the prospective mesoderm undergoes epithelial folding and extension; mesoderm cell nuclei undergo basal migration; the nucleus functions as a cellular compartmentalizer and intracellular organizer; nuclear relocation organizes the cell cytoskeleton and RhoGEF2 distribution; mesoderm epithelial cells establish a lateral, planar-polarized junctional tier formed by lateral actomyosin that initiates cell intercalation for convergence–extension.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
